The change targets `goal_field`, which the update gene calls each turn. When two or more enemy champions are within 6 tiles, the walk field routes around enemy-occupied tiles (minus the goals themselves) and uses the goals as the stop set. Otherwise it keeps the plain goal field. Retreat behaviour is unchanged.

```python
@gene("s3b", "goal field that routes around enemy tiles when 2+ enemies are within 6; plain goal field otherwise; spawn when retreating", parents=["s3"])
def goal_field(retreat: Bool) -> Field:
    if retreat:
        return field(my_spawn())
    g = goals()
    threats = count(1 for u in enemies() if dist(u.pos, me().pos) <= 6)
    if threats >= 2:
        return field_avoid(g, enemy_tiles() - g, g)
    return field(g)
```

